{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#990","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#990","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#990\",\"parent_revision\":\"d6f9cd31c68166465b793fcd52fcb635c4654b8c7e1a2f6a20f12e9c56b5a935\",\"root_revision\":\"d6f9cd31c68166465b793fcd52fcb635c4654b8c7e1a2f6a20f12e9c56b5a935\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe complete-implementation skill defines 6 sequential quality gate phases (code review, feature verification, integration check, doc drift audit, doc update, context refinement). None of these phases have mechanical enforcement \u2014 no SAM state tracking, no hooks, no checkpoint files. An agent can skip any subset of phases and proceed directly to applying the status:verified label because nothing checks that all phases ran. This was observed in session completing #979 where the agent ran 2 of 6 phases and committed. The implement-feature skill does not have this problem because it uses sam_ready/sam_claim/sam_state MCP calls plus a SubagentStop hook to gate each task. The complete-implementation skill uses prose instructions only.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Enforce complete-implementation quality gate phases\\n\\nGoal: Add mechanical enforcement so complete-implementation quality gate phases cannot be skipped.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. What the 6 phases are and what agents they invoke | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-checker verified 6 phases in complete-implementation/SKILL.md lines 109-197\\n2. SAM MCP tool API capabilities (sam_create, sam_claim, sam_state, sam_ready) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: sam_create schema confirms required fields: task, title, status, agent, dependencies, priority, complexity\\n3. How implement-feature enforces its task loop | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-checker verified sam_ready/sam_claim/sam_state + SubagentStop hook in implement-feature/SKILL.md lines 9-60\\n4. Hook infrastructure patterns (SubagentStop, PostToolUse) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-checker verified SubagentStop handling in task_status_hook.py lines 446-503\\n5. Whether SAM schema supports quality-gate tasks | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: sam_create MCP tool schema shows tasks_yaml accepts list of task dicts with all required fields \u2014 quality gate phases fit the existing model\\n6. How task_status_hook.py records completion | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-checker verified SubagentStop handler marks tasks complete\\n7. Whether checkpoint file patterns exist | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Grep found dispatch_schema/gates.py, T0/TN bookend verification files, BookendVerification model in sam_schema/core/models.py\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 5: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by orchestrator reading sam_create MCP schema)\\n- Condition 7: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by orchestrator grep for checkpoint patterns)\\n\\nNew findings from swarm:\\n- Impact-analyst identified 38 affected files across 5 systems\\n- Fact-checker verified all 5 claims (5 VERIFIED, 0 REFUTED)\\n- No new MISSING conditions discovered\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 7\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (create or modify quality gate flow)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 Rewrite Phases 1-6 to create SAM quality-gate tasks instead of prose-only orchestration; add task-file address resolution for gate tasks; add status checking before final label application\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 Add optional `phase_number: int` and `phase_type: str` fields to Task model to support quality-gate-specific task classification\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 MCP server must support quality-gate task creation (extend sam_create logic or add new endpoint)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 Hook must record phase checkpoint completion; add new hook event type for phase-completion (may extend existing SubagentStop or create new Phase-Complete event)\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read quality gate results)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Update line 154 to invoke complete-implementation properly; may need to read phase checkpoint file before proceeding\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` \u2014 May need updates if quality-gate tasks require special handling during claim/state transitions (read to verify impact after Phase 1 fix is drafted)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 May need to handle phase checkpoint data when syncing to GitHub (read to verify after other changes)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github.py` \u2014 May need to record phase completion status on sub-issues (read to verify impact)\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `.claude/rules/local-workflow.md` \u2014 Phase 3 \\\"Quality Gates\\\" section (lines 237-299) documents prose-only orchestration; must rewrite to describe SAM-task-based phases with checkpoint gates\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 Data flow diagram must show phase tasks being created, claimed, and gated via sam_claim/sam_state/sam_ready\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/plan-artifact-lifecycle.md` \u2014 May reference quality gate phases; verify and update if stale\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 May need new section documenting quality-gate task structure (phase_number, phase_type fields)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md` \u2014 Documents input/output contract; may need clarification on how phase tasks differ from regular tasks\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md` \u2014 Documents when it runs (Phase 2); verify it correctly reads phase metadata\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/integration-checker.md` \u2014 Documents Phase 3; verify phase metadata usage\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/doc-drift-auditor.md` \u2014 Documents Phase 4; verify phase metadata usage\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/service-docs-maintainer.md` \u2014 Documents Phase 5; verify phase metadata usage\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/context-refinement.md` \u2014 Documents Phase 6; verify phase metadata usage\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` frontmatter hooks \u2014 May need new hook event or hook configuration to gate phase transitions\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` / `pyproject.toml` \u2014 No changes needed unless quality-gate task creation adds new validation rules\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md` \u2014 Clarify that Phase 1 runs as a SAM task with sam_claim/sam_state enforcement (not prose-only instructions)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md` \u2014 Clarify Phase 2 readiness gating via sam_ready; add instruction to check prerequisite phase completion\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/integration-checker.md` \u2014 Add instruction to claim Phase 3 task via sam_claim before starting work\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/doc-drift-auditor.md` \u2014 Add instruction for Phase 4 task claiming and state transitions\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/service-docs-maintainer.md` \u2014 Add instruction for Phase 5 task claiming and state transitions\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/context-refinement.md` \u2014 Add instruction for Phase 6 task claiming; clarify this is the final phase before checkpoint verification\\n\\n### Test Coverage\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py` \u2014 Existing; verify it covers complete-implementation flow; may need new test for quality-gate phase gating\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server_mcp.py` \u2014 Existing SAM MCP server tests; may need new test case for quality-gate task creation\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_query.py` \u2014 Existing task query tests; verify ready-task logic handles phase dependencies correctly\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_models.py` \u2014 Existing model tests; add test for new phase_number/phase_type fields on Task model\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/tests/` \u2014 New tests needed for phase-checkpoint hook behavior (may not exist yet)\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n**SAM Task File & Schema:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 Task model (must support phase metadata)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py` \u2014 Query operations (sam_claim, sam_state, sam_ready already exist)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 MCP server (exposes sam_* tools)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py` \u2014 Dependency graph resolution (must handle phase task dependencies correctly)\\n\\n**Quality Gate Agents:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md` \u2014 Phase 1 agent (invokes code-reviewer from language manifest or fallback)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-verifier.md` \u2014 Phase 2 agent\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/integration-checker.md` \u2014 Phase 3 agent\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/doc-drift-auditor.md` \u2014 Phase 4 agent\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/service-docs-maintainer.md` \u2014 Phase 5 agent\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/context-refinement.md` \u2014 Phase 6 agent\\n\\n**Hook Infrastructure:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 Marks tasks COMPLETE; must extend to record phase completions\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` frontmatter hooks \u2014 Configuration; may need extension for phase-completion events\\n\\n**Orchestration Skills:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 Main quality-gate orchestrator (PRIMARY TARGET for rewrite)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Calls complete-implementation at end of execution loop (caller, may need minimal change)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` \u2014 Launches individual tasks; used by both implement-feature and complete-implementation (no change expected)\\n\\n**Backlog Integration:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 Backlog MCP server (may need phase checkpoint handling)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github.py` \u2014 GitHub sync (may need to record phase completion on sub-issues)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` \u2014 Backlog item workflow (may need to read phase checkpoint before closing item)\\n\\n**Supporting Documentation:**\\n- `.claude/rules/local-workflow.md` \u2014 SAM workflow specification (describes current prose-only model; must be updated)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 Workflow diagram (must show quality-gate task flow)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 Task format spec (may need new section for quality-gate task fields)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 Plugin documentation (may reference quality gates; verify if stale)\\n\\n**Connections & Data Flow:**\\n1. `complete-implementation` reads task file and plan address\\n2. Creates quality-gate tasks via `sam_create` (new logic) or appends to existing plan\\n3. Uses `sam_ready` to get first ready phase task\\n4. Uses `sam_claim` to mark phase task IN_PROGRESS\\n5. Delegates to phase agent (code-reviewer, feature-verifier, etc.)\\n6. Hook records phase completion via `sam_state` with COMPLETE status\\n7. Loop repeats via `sam_ready` until all 6 phases complete\\n8. Final checkpoint verification ensures all phases ran\\n9. Only then applies `status:verified` label via backlog MCP\\n\\n**Risk Areas:**\\n- Phase dependency graph must be correct (T0 \u2192 Phase1 \u2192 Phase2 \u2192 ... \u2192 Phase6 \u2192 TN if bookend tasks exist)\\n- Hook timing: SubagentStop must fire after agent finishes, before complete-implementation loop continues\\n- Checkpoint file or state field must be durable (survive across skill invocations within same orchestrator context)\\n- Status:verified label must not be applied if any phase is BLOCKED or skipped\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **enforce complete-implementation quality gate phases with sam tasks and hook checkpoints** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 agent self-reported skipping 4 of 6 mandatory phases with no mechanical blocker\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-22)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nAlways reproducible. Invoke /complete-implementation on any feature plan file. The agent executing it has discretion to run phases in any order, skip phases, or stop early. No gate prevents this because the skill contains prose instructions only. This is not a timing issue \u2014 it is an architectural gap. Observed in session completing #979: agent self-reported running only 2 of 6 phases before committing and applying status:verified.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP0 \u2014 process integrity. The quality gate system is the final verification boundary before features are marked verified. If phases can be skipped, the verified label loses all meaning. Every feature verified through /complete-implementation since the skill was created may have had incomplete verification.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nEvery feature implementation that went through /complete-implementation since the skill was created may have had one or more of the 6 phases skipped. Because there is no mechanical gate, it is impossible to know which items completed all phases and which did not without manual audit. The status:verified label may have been applied to items that had incomplete verification. This undermines both the quality gate system and the trust in the verified label across all completed features.\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\nPrimary: plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md \u2014 Rewrite to use SAM task loop for quality gate phases, replacing prose-only orchestration with sam_create/sam_ready/sam_claim/sam_state gating.\\n\\nSecondary: plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py \u2014 Extend SubagentStop handler to record phase task completion with checkpoints.\\n\\nSecondary: plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py \u2014 Add optional phase_number and phase_type fields to Task model for quality-gate metadata.\\n\\nSecondary: .claude/rules/local-workflow.md \u2014 Update Phase 3 (Quality Gates) section from prose-only to SAM-task-based description.\\n\\nTertiary: plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md \u2014 Update data flow diagram to show phase task creation, claiming, and gating.\\n\\nTertiary: Agent files (code-reviewer, feature-verifier, integration-checker, doc-drift-auditor, service-docs-maintainer, context-refinement) \u2014 Add instructions to use sam_claim before starting phase work and sam_state to mark completion.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nEach quality gate phase (1\u20136) is modeled as a SAM task within the feature plan file. Phases are linked via dependencies: Phase 1 \u2190 Phase 2 \u2190 Phase 3 \u2190 Phase 4 \u2190 Phase 5 \u2190 Phase 6. The complete-implementation skill uses sam_ready to surface only the next phase when all prior phases are COMPLETE. When a phase agent finishes, a SubagentStop hook marks the phase task COMPLETE and records a checkpoint timestamp. A final verification step reads the SAM plan and confirms all 6 phase tasks are COMPLETE before the status:verified label is applied. If any phase is BLOCKED, NOT_STARTED, or missing, the verification step blocks label application with a clear error message listing which phases are incomplete.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Each of the 6 quality gate phases is modeled as a SAM task with sequential dependencies (Phase N blocks on Phase N-1 completion)\\n- [ ] Phase tasks use sam_claim before execution to prevent duplicate dispatch\\n- [ ] Phase tasks use sam_state to mark completion after the phase agent finishes\\n- [ ] A SubagentStop or equivalent hook records phase completion timestamps in the SAM task\\n- [ ] The \\\"Apply status:verified Label\\\" step checks all 6 phase tasks are COMPLETE before proceeding\\n- [ ] If any phase task is BLOCKED or not COMPLETE, label application is blocked with a message listing incomplete phases\\n- [ ] Existing complete-implementation behavior is preserved \u2014 same agents run in same order, same outputs\\n- [ ] Tests verify that attempting to skip a phase blocks the verified label\\n- [ ] Tests verify that completing all phases unblocks the verified label\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\nKey reference implementations:\\n- plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md \u2014 Reference pattern for SAM task loop with sam_ready/sam_claim/sam_state enforcement (lines 44\u2013154)\\n- plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md \u2014 Reference for sam_claim usage and task claiming logic\\n- plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py \u2014 Reference for SubagentStop hook handling and timestamp recording\\n- .claude/rules/local-workflow.md \u2014 Phase 2 \\\"Execution\\\" section (lines 120\u2013190) documents the implement-feature loop pattern; Phase 3 must adopt similar structure\\n- plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py \u2014 Task model definition; reference for where to add phase metadata fields\\n- plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_query.py \u2014 Reference test patterns for sam_ready with dependencies\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- SAM MCP server (sam_create, sam_claim, sam_state, sam_ready) \u2014 already exists and used by implement-feature\\n- Hook infrastructure (SubagentStop hook type) \u2014 already exists and used by implement-feature\\n- Task model schema with dependency support \u2014 already exists in sam_schema\\n- Backlog MCP server (for status:verified label application) \u2014 already exists\\n- All 6 quality gate agents (code-reviewer, feature-verifier, integration-checker, doc-drift-auditor, service-docs-maintainer, context-refinement) \u2014 already exist\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium-High. Primary work is rewriting complete-implementation SKILL.md from prose-only phase orchestration to a SAM task loop analogous to implement-feature (estimate: 200-300 lines of new logic in SKILL.md). Hook extension to record phase checkpoints is incremental \u2014 likely 50-100 lines added to task_status_hook.py. Schema changes (adding phase metadata fields to Task model) are minimal. Documentation updates to local-workflow.md, workflow-architecture-diagram.md, and agent files are mechanical once the primary changes are done. Test coverage is additive \u2014 new tests to verify phase gating, no changes to existing tests.\\n\\n### Architectural Exclusions (ADR-002, ADR-005)\\n\\nThe following items from initial grooming were excluded by the architect spec:\\n- `sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 Task model NOT modified; existing fields sufficient for QG tasks (ADR-002)\\n- `sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 sam_create reused as-is; no new endpoint needed (ADR-002)\\n- `task_status_hook.py` \u2014 existing SubagentStop handling works for QG phases dispatched via /start-task (ADR-002)\\n- 6 quality-gate agent files \u2014 agents invoked via /start-task which handles claiming; agents themselves unchanged (ADR-002)\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read quality gate results)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 calls complete-implementation; no changes needed (verified: invocation interface unchanged)\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (create or modify quality gate flow)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 primary rewrite to SAM task loop (T05)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 NEW module: creates QG plan YAML (T02)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py` \u2014 extend addressing to support QG prefix (T01)\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n- [ ] No Python API for creating QG-prefixed plans \u2014 `create_plan` always writes `P{NNN}-` prefix. Tests use `create_plan_file` workaround. Need `create_qg_plan` function or sam_create extension in follow-up. (reported by T04-worker on T04)\\n- [ ] T5 SKIPPED whitelist enforcement lives in SKILL.md prose (T05), not in code \u2014 integration test validates data model contract only, not the gate itself (reported by T04-worker on T04)\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `.claude/rules/local-workflow.md` \u2014 Phase 3 section needs rewrite (T06)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 needs new phase task flow (T07)\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\nmissing-guardrail \u2014 the skill relies on prose compliance with no enforcement mechanism. An agent reading phase instructions can choose to skip any subset of the 6 phases because nothing prevents it. The complete-implementation skill defines phases but does not gate them via SAM state transitions or hook-based checkpoints. Contrast with implement-feature, which uses sam_ready/sam_claim/sam_state to create a mechanical loop that only surfaces the next task when the prior one completes.\\n\\n### Test Coverage\\n\\n- `tests/test_quality_gates.py` \u2014 NEW: unit tests for quality_gates.py (T03)\\n- `tests/test_qg_integration.py` \u2014 NEW: integration tests for QG plan creation and dispatch (T04)\\n\\n## Fact Check Results 2026 03 22\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Claim 1: complete-implementation skill defines 6 sequential quality gate phases\\n**Evidence**: plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md lines 109-197\\n- Phase 1: Code Review (109-163)\\n- Phase 2: Feature Verification (165-174)\\n- Phase 3: Integration Check (177-179)\\n- Phase 4: Documentation Drift Audit (183-185)\\n- Phase 5: Documentation Update (189-191)\\n- Phase 6: Context Refinement (195-197)\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED \u2713\\n\\n### Claim 2: None of these phases have mechanical enforcement\\n**Evidence**: plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md\\n- Frontmatter (1-10): No hooks field\\n- Phases 1-6: Agent launches only, no sam_claim/sam_state/sam_ready between phases\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED \u2713\\n\\n### Claim 3: implement-feature uses sam_ready/sam_claim/sam_state plus SubagentStop hook\\n**Evidence**: plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md\\n- Lines 9-13: SubagentStop hook declared\\n- Lines 44, 60: sam_status and sam_ready MCP calls present\\n- sam_claim/sam_state delegated to start-task skill, not called directly\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED \u2713 (with clarification: sam_claim/sam_state are in start-task, not implement-feature)\\n\\n### Claim 4: SAM MCP server supports sam_create\\n**Evidence**: System MCP server declarations, sam_create tool listed in available tools\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED \u2713\\n\\n### Claim 5: task_status_hook.py handles SubagentStop to mark tasks complete\\n**Evidence**: plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py\\n- Lines 446-503: handle_subagent_stop() function\\n- Line 492: sam_update_status() call marks task COMPLETE with timestamp\\n- Line 503: Calls sync_completion_to_github() after status update\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED \u2713\\n\\n**Summary**: 5 claims verified, 0 refuted, 0 inconclusive\\n</div>\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| feature-context | plan/feature-context-enforce-quality-gate-phases.md | current | feature-researcher | 2026-03-22T13:42:12.050586+00:00 |\\n| codebase-analysis | plan/codebase/patterns.md | current | codebase-analyzer | 2026-03-22T13:44:21.892793+00:00 |\\n| architect | plan/architect-enforce-quality-gate-phases.md | current | python-cli-design-spec | 2026-03-22T13:50:45.457534+00:00 |\\n| task-plan | plan/P990-enforce-quality-gate-phases.yaml | current | swarm-task-planner | 2026-03-24T16:20:04Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a7543d03126787688387681e2aee75a97a2b36c3b2ed227b02db08a2284efaec\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVWW-PQ\"}"}